    "SHARED, EXTERNALLY FIXED PAIRING-TRANSCRIPT TEST VECTORS (review 2 §P0.4).",
    "",
    "Read by:",
    "  - protocol/typescript/src/crypto/pairing-transcript.ts",
    "  - app/lib/core/crypto/pairing_transcript.dart",
    "  - strideterm: electron/backend/mobile/mobile-crypto.ts (hand mirror)",
    "",
    "The fingerprint commits to the desktop public key, so a control plane that returns a",
    "different key cannot match the digits the human is looking at. The SAS commits to BOTH",
    "sides’ keys and device ids, so the two screens can only agree if both ends hold the same",
    "two keys.",
    "",
    "Cases 2 and 3 are the negative properties as data: changing only the key, or only the device",
    "id, must move both values.",
    "",
    "The keyProof/grantCommitment/approvalTranscriptHash fields are review 3 §P0.1: the claim-time",
    "proof that the claiming device holds the private key behind its published public key and",
    "scanned this desktop’s QR, the digest of the grants the server copied from the invitation, and",
    "the transcript approvePairing recomputes before it will activate anything. Cases 2 and 3 pin",
    "the same negative property for all three: substituting a key or a device id moves every value.",
    "",
    "sessionKeyBase64 is a fixed literal, not an X25519 output — key agreement itself is pinned by",
    "protocol/test-vectors/x25519-hkdf-aead.json, and mixing the two would make a failure here",
    "ambiguous between \"wrong HMAC\" and \"wrong ECDH\".",
    "",
    "Regenerate with: node scripts/generate-aad-vectors.mjs"
  ],
